n  people on the street was passing by we  were begging them you know to help us to  bring it in here Victor's colleagues  Stefan and Zoran helped carry a few  crates up from the basement the books  are being donated to a prison in  Belgrade the crates will be loaded into  this old car which often breaks down but  logic can't afford a new car this is the  home of Lhasa Chaz parents a few hundred  metres from the school in 2010 this is  where he founded the Association ugly  gut the cornerstone of the library  project the Association sponsors a book  and travel museum he doesn't earn any  money from it  Lhasa is a lawyer by profession and  invests almost everything here ins in  this project he also inherited a large  sum and he put that into the book  project too large could afford to live  comfortably but he spends his money on  books his parents don't quite understand  that it's love for books and culture and  literature and believe that we are doing  something it is truly important not only  for this country but it has even bigger  importance broader report importance for  the world and at least for this region  Mozza jazz project now receives  financial support from a few wealthy  donors the extra money could help the  museum grow to 10 rooms la such conduct  guided tours through the collection he  wants the project to become a cultural  beacon for the entire Balkan region his  collection already rivals that of the  country's biggest libraries  nice fragrance yes but it'll change over  time Serbia's government institutions  don't seem very interested in lazarus'  work in fact they've ignored it some  visitors have criticized that like  culture journalist Ivana mackovic  why are the collections of famous  artists like the actor Pavlovic or the  famous poet Miu drug pavlovic on display  here and not in the National Library or  the National Film Archive but if they're  in safe hands here and visitors can see  and touch them which is very unusual  then why not Josh Turner this is a  refugee shelter in bhagavad yeah  60 kilometers south of Belgrade la  search will occasionally drop off some  books here most of them in foreign  languages here are some books  books offer a welcome diversion from the  monotonous daily routine at the refugee  shelter fatima from Shiraz in Iran is  pleased to receive a book in her native  language Farsi this place has its  problems  but we can try to make the most of it by  keeping busy with things like reading  more than a hundred refugees live at the  shelter many are from Afghanistan or  Iran la search doesn't receive a lot of  books in Farsi but when he does he  brings most of them here you know it is  very important for intellectuals and  also for children to have attacks with  their own culture with their own  indentity it also makes them feel more  welcomed here it makes them feel like at  home so I think it is very important for  them yes hello dr. Lesage who's calling  hello can you hear me  a little later Lisette returns to  Belgrade he's trying to secure an  unusually large donation of books but he  has to be faster than the public  libraries and he is most of the time but  if he doesn't move quickly the  collection will be given to another  institution or the books may even end up  in the garbage dump  oh this donation what kind of books in  it well this was one of the extremely  famous litter TV and theater critic so  there are there are excellent books  about TV about theater art it's amazing  larges staff are just as crazy about  books as he is they earn only one year  Oh 40 per hour that's just a bit more  than Serbia's minimum wage plus they  work overtime and put in irregular hours  la search has been working on his book  project for eight years now word about  the project has spread and he's getting  more and more calls from people who want  to donate books that had belonged to  deceased relatives his schedule is  pretty hectic whenever he needs a break  la such likes to come to this meadow  near the belgrade fortress it's one of  his favorite spots in his hometown from  here he has a perfect view of where the  Sava river joins the Danube he has  enjoyed visiting the park since he was a  teenager when he came here to meet girls  well it's a place where I spend most of  my teenage years like after school my  school is in nearby we would come here  and hang out here so I have a lot of  nice memories la searches house is also  his office and a place to store books  but the fact that he's put all of his  money time and energy into the book  project has had a negative effect on his  personal life three years ago his  fiancee left him  they'd been together for some time but  she said she just couldn't take it  anymore  because there was no money not only for  workers there was no money for fuel if  someone donates books I would you know  put the books in the car and would not  have enough fuel to bring them here and  there was not enough money women for  food I mean we weren't actually hungry  but it was always you know problematic  if it will be enough for everything or  not la Serge believes that his book  project is carrying on a family  tradition his great-grandfather loved  books and some of his ancestors even  founded a library but the fact remains  that he no longer has much room for  himself in his own house still that  doesn't bother him I give everything I  have and most of the people in obligate  the founders even the workers they  actually have to invest themselves to  keep this project running at this  perception they're celebrating the  addition of some new storage rooms la  stitch has made a name for himself in  literary circles the guests here include  several prominent writers and other  well-known people it's networking for a  good cause preserving books  [Music]  Victor logic in another step toward his  goal of building a huge library but he  also knows that he's got a lot of work  ahead of him  [Music]

